course: dictionary
lesson: 4566
title: A row of bushes called a hedgerow
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hedgerow is a row of bushes, shrubs and small trees growing along the edge of a field or a country lane. Context helps you find this. Toad's list names «the open road, the dusty highway, the heath, the common, the hedgerows», so a hedgerow is part of the countryside you travel through.
explain: The Badger clue helps too: you usually had to catch him «along a hedgerow». You can walk along a hedgerow and find animals in it. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: "you usually had to catch him along a row of bushes at the edge of a field" still makes sense.
explain: Rabbits in the hedgerows «held up their fore-paws» in surprise, so hedgerows are places where animals live and can be seen. When you meet a new word, ask what would fit there, then test your idea in the sentence.
fact: A hedgerow is a row of bushes, shrubs and small trees along the edge of a field or a country lane.
fact: Hedgerows are typical of the British and Irish countryside.
fact: Birds nest in hedgerows, and hedgehogs and dormice hide in them.
fact: Blackberries, hawthorn and wild roses often grow in hedgerows.
fact: Many hedgerows were pulled up to make bigger fields, and now people are planting them again.
exercise: Toad names «the hedgerows» with the roads and the heath. Where would you find a hedgerow? | *Along the edge of a field or a country lane | Inside a school hall | In the middle of a town square | Under the sea
exercise: The Badger could be caught «along a hedgerow». What does this tell you about a hedgerow? | It is a kind of boat | It is a type of shop | *It is a place you can walk along | It is a loud noise
exercise: Rabbits in the hedgerows «held up their fore-paws». What does this show about hedgerows? | A busy road for cars | *A place where animals live and can be seen | A place with no plants at all | A river
test: Which animals hide in a hedgerow? | Sharks and whales | *Hedgehogs and dormice | Penguins and polar bears | Camels and lions
test: Which plants grow in hedgerows? | Seaweed and kelp | Cacti and palm trees | Lettuce and carrots | *Blackberries, hawthorn and wild roses
exam: What happened to many hedgerows, and what are people doing now? | They were painted bright colours | They were turned into seaside piers | *They were pulled up for bigger fields, and now people are planting them again | They were moved to the city
